# Story page: shop
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Shop
---
Behind a toadstool there is a shop, kept by a raccoon in a very small hat, who sells nearly everything and explains almost nothing.

'Payment is in XP,' said the raccoon, polishing a jar that did not need polishing. 'There are no refunds, there are no questions, and there is nothing whatsoever to say about the hat.'

{name} did not know what XP was. Within a week it would think of little else. This is called ambition, a word which here means 'a hunger that never finds the bottom of the bowl.'
